{{Documentation/Header}}
A large shutdown button for a bot's user page. The button links to [[Special:Block]] with the block form pre-filled to indefinitely hard-block '''the bot whose page it sits on''' — the target is taken from the page name automatically, so the template needs no target parameter.

Administrators can press it directly; non-administrators are pointed at an admin or Miraheze stewards.

==Syntax==
{{T|Emergency-bot-shutoff|block=1
|v1=name =
|v2=titlename =
|v3=icon =
|v4=buttonsize =
}}

==Example==
<pre>{{Emergency-bot-shutoff|name=UWBot}}</pre>

{| class="dataTable sortable"
! Parameter !! Aliases !! Label !! Description !! Type !! Default !! Status
|-
| <code>name</code> || – || Bot name || Name used in the instruction sentence. || string || the bot ||
|-
| <code>titlename</code> || – || Title noun || Noun used in the heading, as in "Emergency ''bot'' shutoff button". || string || bot ||
|-
| <code>icon</code> || – || Icon || File to use as the button image. || wiki-file-name || File:Shutdown button.svg ||
|-
| <code>buttonsize</code> || – || Button size || Button width in pixels, without the unit. || number || 128 ||
|}

{{Notice
| header = Place it on the bot's own page
| info = The block target comes from the page name, so putting this template anywhere other than the bot's user page will pre-fill a block against the wrong account.
| border = orange
}}

